WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:09.940
What up, B?

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:17.400
This week on Thug Notes, we flyin solo with "Jane Eyre" by Charlotte Brontë.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:21.640
As a kid, Jane Eyre livin with her twisted aunt, Mrs. Reed, and her punk-ass cousins,

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.060
who ain't showin no love for my girl Jane.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.180
After dealin with these haters for years, some righteous doc named Lloyd hooks Jane up

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.000
and convinces Mrs. Reed to send Jane away to get schooled.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.670
But Jane ain’t bout to bounce before givin Mrs. Reed a big ol’ "f**k you."

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:38.420
So Jane arrives at Lowood school,

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:42.400
where some b*tch-ass clergyman named Brocklehurst starts hatin on my girl,

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.540
sayin she ain't nothing but a lyin trick.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:49.520
But Jane’s homie Helen and a righteous teacher named Miss Temple tell Jane they got her back.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.740
When Jane’s sista, Helen, dies from consumption and Miss Temple chunks deuces outta Lowood,

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:59.020
Jane bails and starts hustlin as a governess up in Thornfield Hall,

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:02.500
where some uptown gangsta named Edward Rochester be livin.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.320
Once Jane meets Eddie, they start chillin on the reg.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.120
But meanwhile, some mysterious sh*t starts going down at Thornfield:

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:15.460
crazy laughin, somebody startin a fire in Eddie’s room, and one of the house guests gettin shanked.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.900
Later, crusty Aunt Reed sends the word that she bout to kick the bucket.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.960
Now, Jane’s forgiveness don’t quit — so she goes back home and nurses this ho.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:29.400
When Jane rolls back to Thornfield, Edward proposes, and they plan on shackin up together.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.940
Sh*t gets ridiculous durin the ceremony, when some playa-hater named Mason

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.960
say that Edward is already married.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:41.780
Seems Edward’s wife, Bertha, went wack in the head, and she the one who been wreckin sh*t in Eddie's crib.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:46.600
Jane be straight trippin about Edward actin like a pimp, and so she peaces out of Thornfield.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:51.760
Now Jane be all cashed out, askin for help, til some playas named Rivers take her in —

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.700
turns out they be her cousins!

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.880
And when Jane’s Uncle John dies, he leaves her some mad cash!

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.360
Now, Jane got C-notes by da stack, homie.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.920
Then, Jane starts jonesing for her boy Edward,

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.460
so she drops in on Thornfield and sees that the whole place has been burnt down!

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:12.400
Turns out, Bertha’s twisted ass dun blazed the whole place, then killed herself.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.180
Damn!

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:17.580
Not only that, but Eddie dun lost his sight and his hand during the scuffle.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:23.680
But Jane keeps it real and says, “Hey, blood, I don’t care if you ugly as sh*t. I love you anyway.”

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:30.180
Then, they get married and have a little G of they own.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:34.680
Aight son, if you a hustla, you know that the cribs where Jane been stayin at

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:39.260
symbolize all the bullsh*t women had to deal with in Victorian patriarchal society:

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:44.540
oppression wit Auntie Reed, starvation at Lowood, madness at Thornfield,

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.860
and indifference when kickin it wit da Rivers.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:52.020
But it ain’t til we hear bout Eddie's crazy biddy, Bertha, that Brontë starts doin it big.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:57.480
So, if you forever thuggin, you gotta check out how Brontë makin Bertha Jane’s shadow double, playboy.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.140
All the slangin and bangin that this hoochie be doin up in Eddie’s turf

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:05.480
representin all that rage Jane been keepin inside since her days with Auntie Reed.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:11.520
In fact, it don’t get no realer than Bertha, since she the only one who fightin the power that dun f**ked her over.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:17.400
Cuz on the real, who wouldn’t wanna start tearin sh*t up if you got sold to some stranger for a bit o' cash?

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.600
So, what my girl Charlotte tryna say bout traditional society is:

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.960
why can’t women express they desires without bein called crazy?

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:27.460
Yo, you best get in da zone and listen to this here motif, blood.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:29.440
Brontë be stackin images of nature

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:34.640
to show how Jane’s amped-up emotions go way beyond what’s acceptable for women to be feeling.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:40.660
For example, when Rochester proposes to Jane, it starts stormin all up in there for two straight hours.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:46.520
It’s like she been keepin her feelings in for so long, sh*t goes wild when she's finally able to let it out.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:50.720
You can check how Brontë extends this nature motif to my boy, Eddie, too.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:55.860
After he proposes to Jane, lightin strikes a big-ass tree, splittin it in half.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.540
The two halves of the tree representin Eddie’s divided loyalties —

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:05.320
one to his passion for Jane, and the other  to the law and the church, who ain’t got no love for they union.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:11.160
Brontë also spittin truth about the state of the Victorian woman through the red room Jane gets locked up in.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:17.540
Now, this room full of secret compartments and bloody images, which be associated wit dat oohie!

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:20.760
So, dat red room really be all the isolation and hatin

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.000
dat women gotta deal wit during their development into adulthood.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:30.620
Ya heard? Yo, thanks for chillin wit yo boy,
Sparky. Hit subscribe, and I'll see yo ass next week!

